# Learn more at:
# http://docs.owid.io/projects/etl/architecture/metadata/reference/
meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: Births and fertility rates from national statistics
    description: |-
      This data is compiled by Our World in Data, based on the figures published by national statistics offices, civil registries, and health ministries, for the yearly number of births and the total fertility rate. The data spans 2010 to 2025. We use the figures as published and do not calculate any of them ourselves; the only exception is the United Kingdom’s births for 2022–2025, which are calculated as the sum of those of England and Wales, Scotland, and Northern Ireland. For each year, we use the most recent published figure.

      We include a country or area when all of the following are true:

      1. It is a country or area in the UN’s World Population Prospects (2024 edition), and had at least 1 million people in 2023, according to those estimates.
      2. Its yearly count of births is at least 90% complete. We go by what the country reports, either to the UN ([source](https://unstats.un.org/unsd/demographic-social/crvs/#Completeness)) or in a household survey since 2010 ([source](https://data.worldbank.org/indicator/SP.REG.BRTH.ZS)), unless a later census or survey has shown that the count is less complete than that.
      3. A national government body publishes this yearly count, such as the civil registry, the statistics office, or the health ministry. Model estimates and survey results are not included.
      4. The count is available for at least one year from 2020 onward.
      5. The count covers the same population the UN covers. If the national figures leave out or add areas or groups making up 3% or more of births, the country is not included in our dataset. Below that, we include it with a note.

      The spreadsheet has four tabs: an introduction, the data (with the sources and notes for each year), the sources, and every country or area in the UN’s World Population Prospects 2024, with whether it is included and why not.
    date_published: "2026-11-27"

    # Citation
    producer: Official data collated by Our World in Data
    # NOTE: The snapshot script builds citation_full from the spreadsheet's Data and Sources tabs. Don't edit it by hand.
    citation_full: |-
      Our World in Data (2026). Births and fertility rates from national statistics. Compiled from the published figures of national statistics offices, civil registries, and health ministries: [spreadsheet with the data, sources, and notes for each year, and the reason each country is left out](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1XHOgL1AHnhBqiajL5XuFMwiWLmRWlld-r85jv5R5A8I/edit).

      Sources for each country, with the years each one covers, and notes on the data (the spreadsheet also gives each source's title):

      - Albania: [INSTAT](https://databaza.instat.gov.al:8083/pxweb/en/DST/START__BD__BIRTH/BD0008/) (2010–2025); [INSTAT](https://databaza.instat.gov.al:8083/pxweb/en/DST/START__BD__DI/Indeksi01/) (2010–2025). Notes: 2010–2011: Fertility rate uses population estimates from before the 2023 census, unlike later years.
      - Algeria: [ONS Algérie](https://www.ons.dz/IMG/pdf/CH1_Demographie1962_2020Fr.pdf) (2010–2019); [ONS Algérie](https://www.ons.dz/IMG/pdf/Demographie2019bis.pdf) (2010–2019); [ONS Algérie](https://www.ons.dz/IMG/pdf/Demographie_Alg2020_2023.pdf) (2020–2023). Notes: 2010–2023: Births are by year of registration. 2010–2019: The fertility rate is an ONS estimate.
      - Argentina: [DEIS, Ministerio de Salud](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/serie5nro54.pdf) (2010); [DEIS, Ministerio de Salud](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/serie5nro55.pdf) (2011); [DEIS, Ministerio de Salud](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/serie5nro56.pdf) (2012); [DEIS, Ministerio de Salud](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/serie5nro57.pdf) (2013); [DEIS, Ministerio de Salud](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/serie5nro58.pdf) (2014); [DEIS, Ministerio de Salud](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/serie5numero59.pdf) (2015); [DEIS, Ministerio de Salud](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/serie5nro60.pdf) (2016); [DEIS, Ministerio de Salud](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/serie5nro61.pdf) (2017); [DEIS, Ministerio de Salud](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/serie5nro62.pdf) (2018); [DEIS, Ministerio de Salud](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/serie5numero63.pdf) (2019); [DEIS, Ministerio de Salud](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/serie5numero64_web.pdf) (2020); [Dirección Nacional de Población, Ministerio del Interior](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/2023/10/la_natalidad_y_la_fecundidad_en_argentina_entre_1980_y_2020_0.pdf) (2020); [DEIS, Ministerio de Salud](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/serie_5_nro_65_anuario_vitales_2021_-_web.pdf) (2021); [Dirección Nacional de Población, Ministerio del Interior](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/2023/10/informe_natalidad_2023.pdf) (2021); [DEIS, Ministerio de Salud](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/serie_5_nro_66_anuario_vitales_2022_3.pdf) (2022); [INDEC](https://www.indec.gob.ar/ftp/cuadros/publicaciones/proyecciones_nacionales_2022_2040.pdf) (2022); [DEIS, Ministerio de Salud](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/serie_5_nro_67_anuario_vitales_2023-version_final.pdf) (2023); [DEIS, Ministerio de Salud](https://www.argentina.gob.ar/sites/default/files/serie_5_nro_68_anuario_vitales_2024_v2.pdf) (2024). Notes: 2010–2024: Births are by year of registration. 2020–2021: Fertility rate uses population estimates from before the 2022 census, unlike 2022. 2022: The fertility rate is an INDEC estimate.
      - Armenia: [Armstat](https://armstat.am/en/?nid=82&id=2786) (2010–2024); [Armstat](https://armstat.am/en/?nid=82&id=2446) (2010); [Armstat](https://armstat.am/en/?nid=82&id=2535) (2011); [Armstat](https://armstat.am/en/?nid=82&id=2624) (2012); [Armstat](https://armstat.am/en/?nid=82&id=2705) (2013–2022); [Armstat](https://armstat.am/file/doc/99568918.xls) (2025). Notes: 2010–2022: Fertility rate uses population estimates from before the 2022 census, unlike later years.
      - Australia: [ABS](https://www.abs.gov.au/statistics/people/population/national-state-and-territory-population) (2010–2025); [ABS](https://data.api.abs.gov.au/rest/data/ABS,FERTILITY_AGE_STATE/all?startPeriod=2010) (2010–2025). Notes: 2010–2025: Births are ABS estimates by year of birth, including an allowance for births not yet registered. 2010–2025: The fertility rate is by year of registration. 2025: Number of births is provisional.
      - Austria: [Statistik Austria](https://data.statistik.gv.at/data/OGD_geborene_ext_GEB_1.csv) (2010–2025); [Statistik Austria](https://www.statistik.at/fileadmin/pages/411/OEsterreich_Zeitreihenindikatoren_1961_2025.ods) (2010–2025).
      - Azerbaijan: [State Statistical Committee of the Republic of Azerbaijan](https://www.stat.gov.az/source/demoqraphy/en/002_1en.xls) (2010–2025); [State Statistical Committee of the Republic of Azerbaijan](https://www.stat.gov.az/source/demoqraphy/en/002_3en.xls) (2010–2025). Notes: 2010–2025: Births are by year of registration. 2010–2023: Leaves out Nagorno-Karabakh (about 1–2% of births).
      - Bahrain: [Ministry of Health, Bahrain](https://www.moh.gov.bh/Content/Files/Publications/statistics/HS2014/PDF/Chapters/vital%20statistics_2014.pdf) (2010); [Ministry of Health, Bahrain](https://www.data.gov.bh/explore/dataset/06-total-fertility-rate/) (2010–2024); [Ministry of Health, Bahrain](https://www.data.gov.bh/explore/dataset/01-live-births/) (2011–2024). Notes: 2015–2024: Births include babies born abroad to Bahraini citizens.
      - Belarus: [Belstat](https://dataportal.belstat.gov.by/osids/indicator-info/10101200001) (2010–2019, 2024–2025); [Belstat](https://dataportal.belstat.gov.by/osids/indicator-info/10101200011) (2010–2019, 2024–2025).
      - Belgium: [Statbel](https://statbel.fgov.be/sites/default/files/files/documents/bevolking/5.5%20Geboorten%20en%20vruchtbaarheid/BirthEvo_1830-NL.xls) (2010–2025); [Statbel](https://statbel.fgov.be/en/themes/population/natality-and-fertility) (2010–2022); [Statbel](https://statbel.fgov.be/en/themes/population/natality-and-fertility) (2023); [Statbel](https://statbel.fgov.be/sites/default/files/files/documents/bevolking/5.5%20Geboorten%20en%20vruchtbaarheid/BE_Naissances%20et%20f%C3%A9condit%C3%A9_2024_PRVSR.xlsx) (2024); [Statbel](https://statbel.fgov.be/en/themes/population/natality-and-fertility) (2025). Notes: 2015–2018, 2024–2025: Fertility rate is provisional.
      - Benin: [INStaD (Institut National de la Statistique et de la Démographie), Benin](https://instad.bj/images/docs/insae-publications/annuelles/AS-INSAE/Annee_2024/Annuaire%202024.pdf) (2011, 2013, 2017, 2021); [INSAE (now INStaD), Benin](https://www.instad.bj/images/docs/insae-statistiques/enquetes-recensements/Autres-Enquetes/Autres/RESUME%20DE%20L'ENQUETE%20MICS%202014%20AU%20BENIN.pdf) (2014); [INStaD (Institut National de la Statistique et de la Démographie), Benin](https://instad.bj/images/docs/insae-statistiques/Etat-civil/ANNUAIRE_DES_STAT_DE_L'ETAT_CIVIL_2020.pdf) (2020); [INStaD (Institut National de la Statistique et de la Démographie), Benin](https://instad.bj/images/docs/insae-statistiques/Etat-civil/ANNUAIRE_DES_STAT_DE_L'ETAT_CIVIL_2022.pdf) (2022); [INStaD (Institut National de la Statistique et de la Démographie), Benin](https://instad.bj/images/docs/insae-statistiques/Etat-civil/ANNUAIRE_DES_STAT_DE_L'ETAT_CIVIL_2024.pdf) (2023–2024). Notes: 2011, 2014, 2017, 2021: The fertility rate is from a household survey. 2013: The fertility rate is from the census. 2020, 2022–2024: Births are birth declarations to the national register of persons, mostly made at health facilities, not completed civil registrations.
      - Bolivia: [INE Bolivia (SERECI civil registry data)](https://nube.ine.gob.bo/index.php/s/fps0vBJBd7R0c34/download) (2010–2025); [INE Bolivia](https://nube.ine.gob.bo/index.php/s/tXaTJM8geaZhUSf/download) (2016, 2023); [INE Bolivia](https://nimbus.ine.gob.bo/index.php/s/PaHRM4KgJXASM6n/download) (2024). Notes: 2010–2025: Births are registrations of babies under 1, by year of registration. 2016, 2023: The fertility rate is from a household survey. 2024: The fertility rate is an INE estimate. 2025: Number of births is provisional.
      - Bosnia and Herzegovina: [Agency for Statistics of Bosnia and Herzegovina](https://bhas.gov.ba/data/Publikacije/Bilteni/2026/DEM_00_2025_TB_1_BS.pdf) (2010–2025). Notes: 2010–2011: Fertility rate uses an older population base than later years.
      - Brazil: [Ministério da Saúde (SINASC)](http://tabnet.datasus.gov.br/cgi/deftohtm.exe?sinasc/cnv/nvuf.def) (2010–2025); [IBGE](https://anuario.ibge.gov.br/images/aeb/2025/s2/2_pdf/s2t1303.pdf) (2010–2023). Notes: 2010–2025: Births are health ministry birth records, not civil registrations. 2010–2023: The fertility rate is an IBGE estimate. 2025: Number of births is provisional.
      - Bulgaria: [National Statistical Institute, Bulgaria](https://www.nsi.bg/en/statistical-data/217/693) (2010–2025); [National Statistical Institute, Bulgaria](https://www.nsi.bg/en/statistical-data/215/687) (2010–2025). Notes: 2010–2025: Births include babies born abroad to people with an address in Bulgaria; late registrations count in the year registered. 2010–2021: Fertility rate uses population estimates from before the 2021 census, unlike later years.
      - Canada: [Statistics Canada](https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/t1/tbl1/en/tv.action?pid=1310041601) (2010–2025); [Statistics Canada](https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/t1/tbl1/en/tv.action?pid=1310041801) (2010–2025). Notes: 2025: Number of births is provisional.
      - Chile: [INE Chile](https://www.ine.gob.cl/docs/default-source/nacimientos-matrimonios-y-defunciones/cuadros-estadisticos/series-hist%C3%B3ricas/series-vitales-1992-2025(p).xlsx) (2010–2025). Notes: 2024–2025: Births and fertility rate are provisional.
      - China: [National Bureau of Statistics (NBS), China](https://www.stats.gov.cn/sj/pcsj/rkpc/6rp/html/B0604a.htm) (2010); [National Health Commission (NHC), China](https://www.nhc.gov.cn/mohwsbwstjxxzx/tjtjnj/202604/155ab0f98dfd4b12874f08f828df1452.shtml) (2016–2024); [National Bureau of Statistics (NBS), China](https://www.stats.gov.cn/sj/pcsj/rkpc/7rp/zk/html/B0604.jpg) (2020). Notes: 2010, 2020: The fertility rate is from the census. 2016–2024: Births are hospital delivery reports to the health ministry, not civil registrations.
      - Colombia: [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/index.php/estadisticas-por-tema/salud/nacimientos-y-defunciones/nacimientos/nacimientos-2010) (2010); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/index.php/estadisticas-por-tema/salud/nacimientos-y-defunciones/nacimientos/nacimientos-2011) (2011); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/index.php/estadisticas-por-tema/salud/nacimientos-y-defunciones/nacimientos/nacimientos-2012) (2012); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/index.php/estadisticas-por-tema/salud/nacimientos-y-defunciones/nacimientos/nacimientos-2013) (2013); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/files/operaciones/EEVV/bol-EEVV-Nacimientos-IIItrim2023.pdf) (2013); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/index.php/estadisticas-por-tema/salud/nacimientos-y-defunciones/nacimientos/nacimientos-2014) (2014); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/files/operaciones/EEVV/2024/19-dic-2024/bol-EEVV-Nacimientos-2024pr.pdf) (2014); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/index.php/estadisticas-por-tema/salud/nacimientos-y-defunciones/nacimientos/nacimientos-2015) (2015); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/files/operaciones/EEVV/2026/6-feb-2026/bol-EEVV-Isem2025pr.pdf) (2015); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/index.php/estadisticas-por-tema/salud/nacimientos-y-defunciones/nacimientos/nacimientos-2016) (2016); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/files/operaciones/EEVV/2026/24-sep-2026/bol-EEVV-Isem2026pr.pdf) (2016–2025); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/index.php/estadisticas-por-tema/salud/nacimientos-y-defunciones/nacimientos/nacimientos-2017) (2017); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/index.php/estadisticas-por-tema/salud/nacimientos-y-defunciones/nacimientos/nacimientos-2018) (2018); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/index.php/estadisticas-por-tema/salud/nacimientos-y-defunciones/nacimientos/nacimientos-2019) (2019); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/index.php/estadisticas-por-tema/salud/nacimientos-y-defunciones/nacimientos/nacimientos-2020) (2020); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/index.php/estadisticas-por-tema/salud/nacimientos-y-defunciones/nacimientos/nacimientos-2021) (2021); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/index.php/estadisticas-por-tema/salud/nacimientos-y-defunciones/nacimientos/nacimientos-2022) (2022); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/index.php/estadisticas-por-tema/salud/nacimientos-y-defunciones/nacimientos/nacimientos-2023) (2023); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/index.php/estadisticas-por-tema/salud/nacimientos-y-defunciones/nacimientos/nacimientos-2024) (2024); [DANE](https://www.dane.gov.co/index.php/estadisticas-por-tema/salud/nacimientos-y-defunciones/nacimientos/nacimientos-2025) (2025). Notes: 2010–2025: Births are birth certificates filled in at health facilities, not civil registrations. 2019–2021: Births include babies born in Colombia to mothers living abroad (1.4–1.8% of births).
      - Costa Rica: [INEC Costa Rica](https://admin.inec.cr/sites/default/files/2026-04/sepoblacnac1950-2025-01.xls) (2010–2024); [INEC Costa Rica](https://admin.inec.cr/sites/default/files/2025-12/repoblacEV-Panorama%20demogr%C3%A1fico-2024A.pdf) (2010–2024); [INEC Costa Rica](https://admin.inec.cr/sites/default/files/2026-11/rePoblacEV-FMIER-2025web.xlsx) (2025); [INEC Costa Rica](https://admin.inec.cr/sites/default/files/2026-11/rePoblacEV-BID-2025A%20web.xlsx) (2025). Notes: 2010–2025: Births are by year of registration.
      - Croatia: [Croatian Bureau of Statistics](https://web.dzs.hr/PXWeb/pxweb/en/Stanovni%C5%A1tvo/Stanovni%C5%A1tvo__Vitalna%20statistika__Ro%C4%91eni/SV112.px/) (2010–2024); [Croatian Bureau of Statistics](https://web.dzs.hr/PXWeb/pxweb/en/Stanovni%C5%A1tvo/Stanovni%C5%A1tvo__Demografski%20pokazatelji/SD812.px/) (2010–2024); [Croatian Bureau of Statistics](https://podaci.dzs.hr/2026/en/121582) (2025).
      - Cuba: [ONEI](http://www.onei.gob.cu/sites/default/files/publicaciones/2025-07/00-anuario-demografico-2024.pdf) (2010–2024); [ONEI](http://www.onei.gob.cu/sites/default/files/publicaciones/2023-02/0-anuario-demografico-completa-2019_compressed.pdf) (2010); [ONEI](http://www.onei.gob.cu/sites/default/files/publicaciones/2023-02/anuario_demografico-2020compressed.pdf) (2011); [ONEI](http://www.onei.gob.cu/sites/default/files/publicaciones/2023-02/anuario_demografico_2021_compressed.pdf) (2012); [ONEI](http://www.onei.gob.cu/sites/default/files/publicaciones/2023-10/00-anuario-demografico2022.pdf) (2013); [ONEI](http://www.onei.gob.cu/sites/default/files/publicaciones/2024-11/00-anuario-demografico-de-cuba-2023.pdf) (2014); [ONEI](http://www.onei.gob.cu/sites/default/files/publicaciones/2026-07/indicadores-demograficos-2025.pdf) (2025); [MINSAP](https://files.sld.cu/dne/files/2026/10/AES-18-10-26.-Versi%c3%b3n-electr%c3%b3nica.pdf) (2025). Notes: 2021–2025: Fertility rate leaves out people abroad most of the year, unlike earlier years. 2025: Fertility rate is provisional.
      - Czechia: [Czech Statistical Office](https://data.csu.gov.cz/datastat/info/SADA/OBY03) (2010–2025).
      - Denmark: [Statistics Denmark](https://www.statbank.dk/HISB3) (2010–2025); [Statistics Denmark](https://www.statbank.dk/FERT1) (2010–2025).
      - Egypt: [CAPMAS](https://www.capmas.gov.eg:8080/Publication/Pdf/c9cf2878-a6da-4a2d-9ff7-ea95dde6dc2c.pdf) (2010–2025); [Ministry of Health and Population, Egypt, El-Zanaty and Associates, and ICF International](https://dhsprogram.com/pubs/pdf/FR302/FR302.pdf) (2014); [CAPMAS](https://www.capmas.gov.eg:8080/Publication/Pdf/c094ec36-e7c7-4654-bf51-3ce1a39f4381.pdf) (2015); [CAPMAS](https://www.capmas.gov.eg:8080/News/Pdf/02f26b46-0711-4e12-be00-ee1fad224167.pdf) (2016); [CAPMAS](https://www.capmas.gov.eg:8080/Publication/Pdf/2c1501e0-5451-49f3-a48a-20f9e96347ce.pdf) (2017); [CAPMAS](https://www.capmas.gov.eg:8080/Publication/Pdf/e9e3d6e7-c70d-48a6-a613-638ae5897da7.pdf) (2018). Notes: 2014: The fertility rate is from a household survey. 2015–2025: The fertility rate is a CAPMAS estimate.
      - Estonia: [Statistics Estonia](https://andmed.stat.ee/en/stat/rahvastik__rahvastikunaitajad-ja-koosseis__demograafilised-pehinaitajad/RV030) (2010–2025); [Statistics Estonia](https://andmed.stat.ee/en/stat/rahvastik__rahvastikunaitajad-ja-koosseis__demograafilised-pehinaitajad/RV033) (2010–2025).
      - Finland: [Statistics Finland](https://pxdata.stat.fi/PxWeb/pxweb/en/StatFin/StatFin__synt/12dj.px/) (2010–2025); [Statistics Finland](https://pxdata.stat.fi/PxWeb/pxweb/en/StatFin/StatFin__synt/12dt.px/) (2010–2025).
      - France: [INSEE](https://www.insee.fr/fr/statistiques/9017867) (2010–2025); [INSEE](https://www.insee.fr/fr/statistiques/8999017?sommaire=8999231) (2010–2025). Notes: 2010–2025: Metropolitan France only, as in the UN data. 2023–2025: Fertility rate is provisional.
      - Germany: [Destatis](https://genesis.destatis.de/datenbank/online/statistic/12612/table/12612-0001) (2010–2025); [Destatis](https://genesis.destatis.de/datenbank/online/statistic/12612/table/12612-0009) (2010–2025). Notes: 2010–2011: Fertility rate uses population estimates from before the 2022 census, unlike later years.
      - Greece: [ELSTAT (Hellenic Statistical Authority)](https://www.statistics.gr/en/statistics/-/publication/SPO03/2025) (2010–2025); [ELSTAT (Hellenic Statistical Authority)](https://www.statistics.gr/documents/20181/18020200/LivingConditionsInGreece_0923.pdf/8658fb65-20e5-3650-b5ec-255404046a2f) (2010); [ELSTAT (Hellenic Statistical Authority)](https://www.statistics.gr/documents/20181/18268733/LivingConditions_0924.pdf/0db19552-7168-ceb3-6bdc-f94c493e45bc) (2011); [ELSTAT (Hellenic Statistical Authority)](https://www.statistics.gr/documents/20181/18511140/LivingConditions_0925.pdf/b278136c-cec8-3551-a8e3-715a0d167ed7) (2012); [ELSTAT (Hellenic Statistical Authority)](https://www.statistics.gr/documents/20181/18740733/LivingConditions_0926.pdf/dee138ac-4ef0-8c12-ee58-31757d902460) (2013); [ELSTAT (Hellenic Statistical Authority)](https://www.statistics.gr/documents/20181/18740733/LivingConditions_1126.pdf/de0859ae-0de7-cbc0-a37e-559791f0f639) (2014–2024). Notes: 2011–2012: Fertility rate uses population estimates from before ELSTAT revised them in December 2025, unlike later years.
