      - Slovakia: [Statistical Office of the Slovak Republic (ŠÚ SR)](https://statdata.statistics.sk/public/ui/dc/domov/data-view/view/om7103rr?lang=sk) (2012–2025); [Statistical Office of the Slovak Republic (ŠÚ SR)](https://statdata.statistics.sk/public/ui/dc/domov/data-view/view/om2009rs?lang=sk) (2012–2025). Notes: 2022–2025: Leaves out births in Slovakia to mothers without permanent residence, mostly refugees from Ukraine (about 1% of births).
      - Slovenia: [Statistical Office of the Republic of Slovenia (SURS)](https://pxweb.stat.si/SiStatData/pxweb/en/Data/-/05J1002S.px) (2010–2025).
      - Spain: [INE (Instituto Nacional de Estadística)](https://www.ine.es/jaxiT3/Tabla.htm?t=48861) (2010–2025); [INE (Instituto Nacional de Estadística)](https://www.ine.es/jaxiT3/Tabla.htm?t=1407) (2010–2025).
      - Sri Lanka: [Department of Census and Statistics, Sri Lanka](https://www.statistics.gov.lk/Resource/en/Population/Vital_Statistics/NumberofBirthsDeathsMarriagesInfantandMaternalDeathRate2000-2025.pdf) (2010–2025); [Registrar General's Department, Sri Lanka](https://www.rgd.gov.lk/web/images/2023/vitalStat/VITAL-STATISTICS-REPORT-2008-2017.pdf) (2010–2013); [Department of Census and Statistics and Ministry of Health, Sri Lanka](https://www.statistics.gov.lk/Resource/en/Health/DemographicAndHealthSurveyReport-2016-Chapter4.pdf) (2016); [Department of Census and Statistics, Sri Lanka](https://www.statistics.gov.lk/Resource/en/Population/CPH_2024/CPH2024_Final_Eng.pdf) (2024). Notes: 2010–2025: Births are by year of registration. 2016: The fertility rate is from a household survey. 2021–2025: Number of births is provisional. 2024: The fertility rate is from the 2024 census.
      - Sweden: [Statistics Sweden (SCB)](https://www.statistikdatabasen.scb.se/pxweb/en/ssd/START__BE__BE0101__BE0101G/BefUtvKon1749/) (2010–2025); [Statistics Sweden (SCB)](https://www.statistikdatabasen.scb.se/pxweb/en/ssd/START__BE__BE0101__BE0101H/FruktsamhetSum/) (2010–2025). Notes: 2015–2017: Leaves out births where neither parent is registered in Sweden, mostly to asylum seekers (about 1–2% of births).
      - Switzerland: [Federal Statistical Office (FSO), Switzerland](https://www.pxweb.bfs.admin.ch/pxweb/de/px-x-0102020204_111/px-x-0102020204_111/px-x-0102020204_111.px) (2010–2025). Notes: 2010–2025: Leaves out births to foreign nationals with permits for less than 12 months and to asylum seekers in Switzerland for less than 12 months.
      - Thailand: [Ministry of Public Health (Strategy and Planning Division), Thailand](https://spd.moph.go.th/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%96%E0%B8%B4%E0%B8%95%E0%B8%B4%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%98%E0%B8%B2%E0%B8%A3%E0%B8%93%E0%B8%AA%E0%B8%B8%E0%B8%82-2567_final.pdf) (2010–2024); [Ministry of Public Health (Bureau of Reproductive Health), Thailand](https://rh.anamai.moph.go.th/web-upload/7x027006c2abe84e89b5c85b44a692da94/tinymce/kpi67/3_11/3_11_1-1-5m.pdf) (2022); [Ministry of Public Health (Bureau of Reproductive Health), Thailand](https://rh.anamai.moph.go.th/web-upload/7x027006c2abe84e89b5c85b44a692da94/tinymce/kpi69/3_16/3_16-1_1.pdf) (2023); [Ministry of Public Health (Bureau of Reproductive Health), Thailand](https://rh.anamai.moph.go.th/web-upload/7x027006c2abe84e89b5c85b44a692da94/tinymce/kpi69/3_16/3_16-1_2.pdf) (2024).
      - Tunisia: [Institut National de la Statistique (INS), Tunisia](https://www.ins.tn/sites/default/files-ftp3/files/publication/pdf/annuaire-2014.pdf) (2010); [Institut National de la Statistique (INS), Tunisia](https://www.ins.tn/sites/default/files-ftp3/files/publication/pdf/Annuaire-2015.pdf) (2011); [Institut National de la Statistique (INS), Tunisia](https://www.ins.tn/sites/default/files-ftp3/files/publication/pdf/annuaire-2016.pdf) (2012); [Institut National de la Statistique (INS), Tunisia](https://www.ins.tn/sites/default/files-ftp3/files/publication/pdf/annuaire-2017.pdf) (2013); [Institut National de la Statistique (INS), Tunisia](https://www.ins.tn/sites/default/files-ftp3/files/publication/pdf/annuaire-2018%20.pdf) (2014); [Institut National de la Statistique (INS), Tunisia](https://www.ins.tn/sites/default/files-ftp3/files/publication/pdf/annuaire-2019%20avec%20lien_2.pdf) (2015); [Institut National de la Statistique (INS), Tunisia](https://www.ins.tn/statistiques/112) (2016–2024); [Institut National de la Statistique (INS), Tunisia](https://www.ins.tn/sites/default/files-ftp3/files/publication/pdf/annuaire-2020%20avec%20lien_5.pdf) (2016); [Institut National de la Statistique (INS), Tunisia](https://www.ins.tn/sites/default/files-ftp3/files/publication/pdf/annuaire-2021avec%20lien_3.pdf) (2017); [Institut National de la Statistique (INS), Tunisia](https://www.ins.tn/sites/default/files-ftp3/files/publication/pdf/annuaire_2022.pdf) (2018); [Institut National de la Statistique (INS), Tunisia](https://www.ins.tn/sites/default/files-ftp3/files/publication/pdf/annuaire-2023avec%20lien.pdf) (2019–2023); [Institut National de la Statistique (INS), Tunisia](https://www.ins.tn/sites/default/files-ftp3/files/publication/pdf/Flash_Projection_de%20la%20Population.pdf) (2024); [Institut National de la Statistique (INS), Tunisia](https://www.ins.tn/sites/default/files-ftp3/files/publication/pdf/bms%20Juillet%202026_3.pdf) (2025). Notes: 2025: Number of births is provisional.
      - Turkmenistan: [State Committee of Turkmenistan on Statistics and UNICEF](https://mics.ipums.org/mics/resources/enum_materials_pdf/report_tm2015a_eng.pdf) (2015); [State Committee of Turkmenistan on Statistics](https://www.stat.gov.tm/storage/publications/pdfs/76/muzhchiny-i-zhenshchiny-turkmenistana.pdf) (2018–2022); [State Committee of Turkmenistan on Statistics and UNICEF](https://mics.ipums.org/mics/resources/enum_materials_pdf/report_tm2019a_eng.pdf) (2019). Notes: 2015, 2019: The fertility rate is from a household survey. 2018–2022: Births are published in thousands, to one decimal.
      - United Arab Emirates: [National Bureau of Statistics (now FCSC), UAE](https://web.archive.org/web/20171209082022/http://www.uaestatistics.gov.ae:80/ReportPDF/%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AA%D9%82%D8%B1%D9%8A%D8%B1%20%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%A7%D8%AD%D8%B5%D8%A7%D8%A6%D9%8A%20%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B3%D9%86%D9%88%D9%8A%202011_111212.pdf) (2010); [National Bureau of Statistics (now FCSC), UAE](https://web.archive.org/web/20151107012241/http://www.uaestatistics.gov.ae:80/ReportPDF/310113_DSS_BD_%20%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D9%88%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%8A%D8%AF%20%D9%88%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%88%D9%81%D9%8A%D8%A7%D8%AA%202011.xlsx) (2011); [Federal Competitiveness and Statistics Centre (FCSC), UAE](https://bayanat.ae/en/Datasets/Dataset-info?id=tletpKGyx-3a66S4fkImXwokY_5ADXNI5nVvdk465R4.) (2012–2014, 2016–2017); [Ministry of Health and Prevention (MOHAP), UAE](https://mohap.gov.ae/documents/20117/1212145/annual+statistics+book_2015_finalupdated_17jul2019.pdf/e684bb36-5658-8535-f1e9-2a8514795a5c) (2015); [Ministry of Health and Prevention (MOHAP), UAE](https://mohap.gov.ae/documents/20117/1212145/registered+live+birth+disterbuted+by+nationality+sex+and+medical+district+2018-en.xlsx/66d8885e-63c3-f6f8-ac6d-a9a122c130fd) (2018); [Ministry of Health and Prevention (MOHAP), UAE](https://mohap.gov.ae/documents/20117/1212145/UAE+Statistical+Annual+Report+2019-240.pdf/892ea9a6-0bde-0454-330a-6cf75eeebc52) (2019); [Ministry of Health and Prevention (MOHAP), UAE](https://mohap.gov.ae/documents/20117/1212145/UAE+Statistical+Annual+Report+2020-417.pdf/0abcd5f8-d8a3-24e9-d17d-1c7aa5642181) (2020); [Ministry of Health and Prevention (MOHAP), UAE](https://mohap.gov.ae/documents/37849/874734/UAE+Statistical+Annual+Report+2021.pdf/e13e370f-a025-7d53-ec8f-b211abfd3071) (2021); [Ministry of Health and Prevention (MOHAP), UAE](https://mohap.gov.ae/documents/37849/874734/UAE+Statistical+Annual+Report+2022.pdf/b08b0cd5-bd15-1940-ce0b-9ffd96dfe67d) (2022); [Ministry of Health and Prevention (MOHAP), UAE](https://mohap.gov.ae/documents/37849/874734/UAE+Statistical+Annual+Report+2023.pdf/484bbd9a-a2ce-f8e5-cb90-c1023269766a) (2023).
      - United Kingdom: [ONS](https://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/populationandmigration/populationestimates/datasets/vitalstatisticspopulationandhealthreferencetables) (2010–2021); [ONS](https://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/populationandmigration/populationprojections/methodologies/nationalpopulationprojectionsfertilityassumptions2024based) (2010–2024); [ONS](https://www.ons.gov.uk/peoplepopulationandcommunity/birthsdeathsandmarriages/livebirths/datasets/birthsinenglandandwalesbirthregistrations) (2022–2025); [NRS](https://nrscotland.gov.uk/publications/adoptions-births-deaths-marriages-and-civil-partnerships-in-scotland-2025-registrar-generals-annual-statistical-tables-of-vital-events/) (2022–2025); [NISRA](https://www.nisra.gov.uk/publications/registrar-general-annual-report-2025-births) (2022–2025). Notes: 2022–2025: Births are the sum of England & Wales, Scotland, and Northern Ireland.
      - United States: [NCHS](https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/data/nvsr/nvsr75/nvsr75-02.pdf) (2010–2024); [NCHS](https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/data/databriefs/db571.pdf) (2025).
      - Uruguay: [INE Uruguay (data from the Ministerio de Salud Pública)](https://www5.ine.gub.uy/documents/ANUARIOS/Anuario%202025/2%20-%20POBLACI%C3%93N/2.3%20Indicadores%20Demogr%C3%A1ficos/2.3.1ok.xls) (2010–2024); [INE Uruguay](https://www5.ine.gub.uy/documents/Demograf%C3%ADayEESS/SERIES%20Y%20OTROS/Estimaciones%20y%20proyecciones/Revisi%C3%B3n%202025/A.2.4%20Indicadores%20de%20fecundidad.xlsx) (2010–2022); [INE Uruguay](https://www5.ine.gub.uy/documents/Demograf%C3%ADayEESS/PDF/Estimaciones%20y%20proyecciones/Estimaciones%20y%20proyecciones%20de%20la%20poblaci%C3%B3n%20de%20Uruguay%202012-2070.pdf) (2023). Notes: 2010–2024: Births are health ministry birth records, not civil registrations.
      - Uzbekistan: [National Statistics Committee of the Republic of Uzbekistan](https://siat.stat.uz/data/223/?lang=en) (2010–2025); [National Statistics Committee of the Republic of Uzbekistan](https://siat.stat.uz/data/665/?lang=en) (2010–2025).

